Round A complete. All five review items fixed, each with its regression.

What changed ([prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc), [safepoint.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc)):

- **Exhaustion escape**: new `php/abandon-to` / `php/call-terminal` terminal escapes that bypass `finally` thunks. `php.sp/exhaust!` now goes through `php/root-fatal`, so a guest `finally { return 7; }` can no longer cancel the fatal.
- **Shutdown path**: `php/run-main` reworked around nested fatal/exit/shutdown escapes. Operational `exc2` from shutdown yields `:php/fatal`, never a catchable Throwable.
- **Budget validation**: `safepoint/program` throws named host-side `ex-info` (`:invalid-budget`) for anything outside non-negative integers.
- **Exit semantics**: `php/exit` uses the root exit continuation — `try { exit(7); } finally { echo 'F'; }` prints no `F`, status preserved through shutdown.
- **Buffer drain**: `php/shutdown!` drains unclosed nested buffers via the proven `ob_end_flush` path after destructors, before global release. `ob_start(); echo 'x';` emits `x`.

Regressions: two new safepoint tests (try/finally exhaustion, shutdown exhaustion, budget validation) plus three `:oracle :pending` P5 fixtures (`:exit-skips-finally`, `:exit-in-finally-wins`, `:unclosed-buffer-drains`).

